,"value":"mutation-guard.ts: each object's own entries are read once per scan into PayloadEntry rows (name, value, path segment, name matches) shared by the leaf pass and the member pass. Every property name is judged by every rule as its own leaf, memoized per distinct name per scan; a name finding carries the new optional SecretGuardFinding.property_name flag and the dedupe key includes it. A flagged name's segment becomes [key n], its index among the object's own entries, in its own finding and every finding under it in both passes. Array indices stay positions. sdk/public-surface.json acknowledges the additive SecretGuardFinding signature change. Documented in docs/MUTATION_INTEGRITY.md."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/close_reason","value":"Payload property names are scanned by every rule, and a flagged name appears in finding paths only as a positional placeholder"}],"before_hash":"35dd582e694df31e76945ebb2f798a1dc9dd4132aff7494bb18dc9a710f60b07","after_hash":"f8c50ed23df4f0859097090146615ec09263903a33f575cd4774ab62b4a7022b","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"completion":{"timestamp":"2026-11-17T09:04:57.856Z","source":"close_time"},"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"13ec45c3fb6b308dc457ec2ba92c8487f5381860d048301f25e4eca83dd48363"}
